  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 157 PM EDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\n- Fair Weather through Labor Day\n\nAn Omega block develops across the CONUS this weekend as the \ncentral U.S. upper high is bookended by cut off lows across the \nNE and NW CONUS. This lowers heights across the central Great \nLakes and allows surface high pressure ridge to build in from the\nnortheast with lower temperatures and dew points. Showers end this\nafternoon and clearing pushed south this evening with it becoming\nnoticeably cooler overnight. Morning lows on Sunday and Monday \nexpected to be in the upper 40s to lower 50s across the northern \nforecast area.\n\n- Chance for showers and Thunderstorms Tuesday and Wednesday\n\nThe surface high retreats east eastward by Tuesday. The Omega \nblock breaks down as a low across the Pacific NW kicks east and \nflattens the upper high, with surface low pressure tracking across\nsouthern Canada. Return flow of moisture and a surface warm front\nshould kick off some showers and thunderstorms late Tuesday into \nWednesday. Another round of storms will be possible as a cold \nfront moves through late Wednesday and shear profiles suggest\nstrong storms are possible if instability is sufficient.",
